Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; TrackingPrevention pins Edge's own default (Balanced) rather than changing behavior -
; written so -VibeCheck reports drift if something flips it. Strict was considered and
; rejected: Microsoft's own doc warns "Some parts of sites might not work."
; BlockThirdPartyCookies is a real behavior change - Edge allows third-party cookies
; by default.
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Edge]
"TrackingPrevention"=dword:00000002
"BlockThirdPartyCookies"=dword:00000001

; Keystroke-level suggestion sources. SearchSuggestEnabled stops every character typed
; in the address bar from being sent to the default search provider for live suggestions;
; local history/favorites suggestions still work (LocalProvidersEnabled is left alone).
"SearchSuggestEnabled"=dword:00000000
"AddressBarTrendingSuggestEnabled"=dword:00000000
"AddressBarClipboardSuggestEnabled"=dword:00000000

; Stops Edge from using browsing history to personalize the sidebar's "top sites"
"PersonalizeTopSitesInCustomizeSidebarEnabled"=dword:00000000

; Edge's Web Speech implementation routes voice through Azure Cognitive Services, so
; voice data leaves the machine - worth disabling even though few sites use it.
"SpeechRecognitionEnabled"=dword:00000000

; Image hover/context-menu lookups sent to Bing
"VisualSearchEnabled"=dword:00000000

; Text typed into web forms sent to Microsoft's cloud Editor service for spell/grammar
; checking; disabling falls back to the local Hunspell engine.
"MicrosoftEditorProofingEnabled"=dword:00000000
"MicrosoftEditorSynonymsEnabled"=dword:00000000

; Near-symbolic in 2026 - most sites ignore it - kept because it costs nothing.
"ConfigureDoNotTrack"=dword:00000001

; Disable personalization of ads, Edge, search and news via browsing data sent to Microsoft
; Disable required and optional diagnostic data about browser usage
; Note: PersonalizationReportingEnabled's own Microsoft doc opens with "This policy
; prevents Microsoft from collecting...", which reads inverted against its own GP title
; ("Allow personalization..."). 0 is correct here (it's a Boolean policy, 0=Disabled
; against the Allow-titled policy) - don't "fix" this to 1.
"PersonalizationReportingEnabled"=dword:00000000
"DiagnosticData"=dword:00000000
"UrlDiagnosticDataEnabled"=dword:00000000
"Edge3PSerpTelemetryEnabled"=dword:00000000
